Subject: [PATCH 35/44] tools: per-module recipes, an opt-in least-error range
 search, and MLX's bitstream for 3, 5 and 6-bit codes

The converter packed whole codes a word, which is right only for 2, 4 and 8 bits; MLX packs a continuous
bitstream. 4-bit output is byte-identical. MTP tensors are skipped so stock Qwen3.5-9B converts too.
